+    // [jetmoto-fork] RECOMPONE_COLLECT_UNMAPPED=1 turns an unmapped call from a
+    // crash into a logged, skipped call. Missing targets here are secondary
+    // entry points inside functions the detector merged, so they can only be
+    // found by running until each one is reached -- one crash per run makes
+    // that a recompile per address. Collecting instead surfaces a whole run's
+    // worth at once. The run's behaviour past the first skip is not
+    // trustworthy; this is for discovery only, never for verification.
